    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488-a2">

                <pb facs="0455" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg373"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department acknowledges the receipt of your letter of November 23, calling
                    attention [etc.].</p>
                <p>I share your regret that the friendly and expanding social and commercial
                    relations and intercourse between the United States and Mexico should in any way
                    imperiled or retarded by propaganda carried on from the American side of the
                    boundary line.</p>
                <p>I am obliged to say however that it is not clear to me in what way the particular
                    question you raise falls within the jurisdiction of the Federal Government, or
                    how the difficulty may be reached by the Federal officials. The Department has,
                    however, copied your letter to the Postmaster General with a view to
                    investigation as to possible violations of the postal laws by the persons
                    responsible for the publications to which you refer.</p>
                <p>It would seem, however, that the matter is entirely within the control of the
                    State authorities, and that if any effective action is to be taken in connection
                    therewith it must be initiated and carried out by them.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
